Project 3: Content-Based AI Recommendation Engine

📌 Executive Summary

Matching user preferences with complex item catalogs or domain roles requires precise pattern alignment rather than arbitrary suggestions. Project 3: AI Recommendation Logic delivers a production-ready Content-Based Filtering Engine designed for personalized recommendation workflows. The system maps raw user skills and domain interests into continuous numerical vector spaces using Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF) and evaluates vector proximity via Cosine Similarity scoring. The architecture is wrapped in an interactive Streamlit Web Interface to provide real-time user ingestion and dynamic feature matching.

🏗️ System Architecture & Algorithmic Pipeline

The core engine executes a 4-stage data processing pipeline:

Stage 1 — Multi-Attribute Input Ingestion: Captures high-dimensional user state (skills, domains, and technical interests) via interactive input controls and aggregates individual attribute strings into a unified text document space.
Stage 2 — Feature Extraction & Vector Mapping (TF-IDF): Raw textual descriptions cannot be directly processed by numerical algorithms. Applies TF-IDF vectorization to construct a vocabulary dictionary and transform text into continuous sparse vectors. Term Frequency (TF) measures keyword occurrence, while Inverse Document Frequency (IDF) scales down ubiquitous stop words while amplifying domain-specific keywords.
Stage 3 — Similarity Scoring Engine (Cosine Distance): Computes vector space proximity between the transformed User Preference Vector and stored Item Profile Vectors using Cosine Distance. It measures the directional alignment between features in high-dimensional space, returning normalized similarity scores bounded between 0% and 100%.
Stage 4 — Ranking, Truncation & UI Rendering: Implements a deterministic sorting pipeline to arrange computed match scores in descending order and truncates results to display the top highest confidence items alongside matched feature keyphrases.
